      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T15:52:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My thinking is that we don\u0027t know what kind of view a consumer might want. Right now we store an framebuffer/attachment view and a texture/sampled view. But someone might want a sampled view with a compatible format, or a view into a multiplanar format that accesses only one plane. I do see the point of not using the resource cache -- it didn\u0027t feel right to me either. If an Image is destroyed we would have orphaned ImageViews. I suppose one solution is to keep the current setup and then if a client class wants to make its own speciality views it can be in charge of maintaining lifetime.",
      "parentUuid": "a413f763_1924a419",
      "revId": "3084cfdbdb03921702500ec871288fcc0133a997",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
